"관측값보다 늦은 추정이 나오면 추정으로 다시 긋는다": recordCooldown observed = now+1h; replace with bumpAgoMinutes 10, bumpCount 3 → expected next - bumped = 96h. bumpedAt = now-10min; next = bumpedAt+96h = now + 95h50m, much later than observed now+1h. So when new estimate is later than observed, use estimate. Interesting: observed is a lower bound, and they replace with new estimate if it's later. Test title: "관측값보다 늦은 추정이 나오면 추정으로 다시 긋는다" - if estimate is later than observed, redraw with estimate. So rule in replaceFromPhone: nextBumpAt = max(observed prior, new estimate). But test A wants prior estimate (not observed) discarded. So need observed flag.

Thus: add column `next_bump_observed` (INTEGER default 0) or separate table. Ensure migration for old DBs. In recordBump: observed = bump.nextBumpAt != null (if explicitly provided). In recordCooldown: observed = 1.

Then ingestedNextBumpAt: given priorNext and priorObserved, bumpedAt, count:
- estimate = new estimate
- if priorObserved: return laterOf(priorNext, estimate)? Test above shows when estimate later than observed, use estimate; test preserving observed later → observed. So max(observed, estimate).
- else return estimate (discard unobserved prior).

But be careful: when card has no bump text (minutes null), bumpedAt = prior, estimate = same as old estimate. Fine.

Also test "끌올 문구가 없으면 마지막 시각을 이어 쓴다": prior recordBump at 2026-10-28T10:00Z, bumpCount 1, next estimate. Card bumpAgoDays null, bumpCount null → bumpCount prior=1, bumpedAt prior, estimate = prior+60h. Works.

Now seed sets next estimate from bumpedAt; observed false. Old DB migration: new column default 0.

Now day-granularity prior bumpedAt preservation. Need to know if card.bumpAgoMinutes used vs bumpAgoDays. When bumpAgoMinutes provided (minutes precision), always compute exact. When only days provided, allow preserving prior if consistent at day level.

Test "`끌올 12시간 전`은 분 단위로 되짚어" uses card with bumpAgoMinutes presumably. Fine.

Implement ingestedBumpedAt:
```ts
function ingestedBumpedAt(card, prior, now) {
  const dayMinutes = card.bumpAgoMinutes === null && card.bumpAgoDays !== null ? card.bumpAgoDays : null;
  if (card.bumpAgoMinutes === null && card.bumpAgoDays === null) return prior;
  const minutes = card.bumpAgoMinutes ?? card.bumpAgoDays! * 1440;
  if (!Number.isFinite(minutes)) return prior;
  const candidate = new Date(now - minutes*60000).toISOString();
  if (card.bumpAgoMinutes === null && prior !== null) {
     // day-level text: keep known time if it's the same number of days back
     const days = Math.round((now - Date.parse(prior)) / 86_400_000);
     if (Number.isFinite(days) && days === card.bumpAgoDays) return prior;
  }
  return candidate;
}
```
But note bumpAgoMinutes may be null and bumpAgoDays could be null; and bumpAgoDays maybe non-integer? It's integer. Note also card.bumpAgoMinutes property might be undefined? DumpCard type. Let's check dump.ts.

