Only this test. But we should be conservative.

Need also fix home land: backToSales should detect home and reopen sales via deep link instead of BACK. Test2 fake: after back from sheet with landHome: mode 'tip' → on BACK: if mode==="home" stray.leftApp=true; mode = (mode==="home"||mode==="kakao")?"kakao":"home". From tip, mode home. Then backToSales loop: dumps home XML (no 판매관리, no 그만두기) → act back → mode home → sets leftApp true and mode kakao. Second iteration dumps kakao, back → mode kakao (not home) → mode = kakao? condition mode==="home" false, so mode = "kakao"? Actually `mode = mode === "home" || mode === "kakao" ? "kakao" : "home"` for kakao → "kakao". leftApp remains true. Then continues 4 times. So need detect home and reopen sales.

How detect home? homeXml has text "홈","채팅","나의 당근","방배4동" package carrot. Could detect via `focusOf` or XML includes "나의 당근" perhaps. In backToSales: if xml contains home markers (e.g., "나의 당근" and not 판매관리) then open deep link. The existing openSales() function already handles not sales by deep link. Could call openSales from backToSales when not on sales after tapping back? But it would reopen after every back attempt. Proposed logic:

```
function backToSales(...) {
  for (let i=0;i<4;i++){
    const xml = dumpXml(...)
    if (isSalesList(xml)) return;
    if (isCarrotHome(xml)) { openSales(serial, exec); continue; } // deep link, no back
    const discard = ...
    ...
    act back...
  }
}
```

But if we check isCarrotHome on any XML not sales, including the bump sheet? The bump sheet likely carrot package and might include "나의 당근"? Probably not. Fake tip XML? `tip` defined where? Let's inspect around 220.

